--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Modal analysis (nModes) of the Gulf of Mexico 80 m lazy-wave cable twisted two turns
-- Driver regression: the cable, clamped and restrained in torsion at both ends, of
-- examples/torsion_lazy_wave_hangoff_twist.dat (illustrative GJ = 50 kN.m^2), with the two turns
-- imposed as the End B pretwist instead of the hang-off roll. The static solve twists the cable
-- by +720 deg; the modes about that twisted equilibrium carry the twist angle of every node
-- (the polar inertia Irn of LINE TYPES), so the table adds PolarShare and dTwist. One 0.1 s step.
